            "summary": "When the model gateway refuses a call because its platform-wide budget for the period is spent, the refusal is named as such rather than reported as a broken gateway, and every such refusal is counted for alerting. A creation step refused this way is not counted against the session, the session waits for the person to send again, and only the cost actually incurred is settled; a skill generation or a criteria suggestion refused this way answers 503 saying nothing was charged and that retrying now is refused too; a judgement refused this way settles as failed with a summary naming the spent budget, that it was not charged and that it will be judged again; the evaluation job is snoozed hourly without spending its attempts, and once the budget recovers a new judgement supersedes the failed one, giving up after a bounded number of snoozes. Every such refusal tells the person the budget recovers at 08:00 Taipei time (UTC midnight) each day, which holds only while the gateway's budget period is one day. A refusal of one key's own budget is not this case and stays an ordinary gateway failure."
